        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Is the number 396 963 842 693 711 divisible by 3?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "No.",
          "worked": "The sum of all the digits is 77. Since $7+7=14$ is not divisible by 3, 77 and the original number are not divisible by 3.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "v2-9731b-p17-practice-slot-10-s10-q-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Which digits in the number could you ignore, and why?\n(Hint: you only need to consider six digits)",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Ignore every occurrence of the digits 3, 6 and 9: each contributes a multiple of 3 to the digit sum. The remaining digits are 8, 4, 2, 7, 1 and 1, whose sum is 23.",
          "worked": "Every occurrence of 3, 6 or 9 contributes a multiple of 3 to the digit sum, so these digits can be ignored. The six remaining digits give\n\n$$\\begin{align*}8+4+2+7+1+1&=23.\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince 23 is not divisible by 3, the original number is not divisible by 3.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      }
    ]
